>[giant-sized discussion]
>okay, i (reluctantly) agree that giants would have an unfair advantage
>in the end game and to that i offer the solution: gaints should be
>super-strong and very clumsy. with every move they should have a probability
>of dropping a considerable fraction of whatever they are carrying. this
>idea would work better if the giants were extremely inefficient at carrying
>things of little size/weight (gold, gems) but very good at carrying things of
>extreme size/weight (enormous rocks). let's say a giant is carrying 500 gems
>and trying to climb out of the dungeon: it succeeds in climbing out but
>unfortunately it scatters 400 of the tiny things on the ground. the giant
>is awarded bonuses only for what it is currently carrying...

Of course you could just simply make it impossible for the player to
leave in any form that would be large enough to be a problem (giants,
purple worms, etc.)  This would eliminate the problem of large,
powerful things carrying more out of the dungeon than would be fair...
And, of course, since the pickaxe can't dig up, then this wouldn't be
a solution.

